4 0 obj
<< /Length 878 >>
stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 2 of 5) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: CS301 Lecture Slides: Concurrency & Deadlocks) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Slide 2: Critical Section Problem Criteria) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (Any valid solution to the critical section problem must satisfy three strict requirements:) Tj T* (1. Mutual Exclusion: If process Pi is executing in its critical section, no other processes can enter.) Tj T* (2. Progress: If no process is executing in its critical section and some wish to enter,) Tj T* (   only processes not in remainder section can participate in the selection.) Tj T* (3. Bounded Waiting: There must be a bound on the number of times other processes are allowed) Tj T* (   to enter their critical sections after a process has made a request to enter.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
5 0 obj
<< /Length 622 >>
stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 3 of 5) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: CS301 Lecture Slides: Concurrency & Deadlocks) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Slide 3: Summary of the Four Coffman Conditions) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (Remember the acronym M-H-N-C:) Tj T* (- Mutual Exclusion \(exclusive ownership\)) Tj T* (- Hold and Wait \(holding while requesting\)) Tj T* (- No Preemption \(cannot steal\)) Tj T* (- Circular Wait \(chain of waiting dependencies\)) Tj T* (ALL 4 conditions MUST be simultaneously true for deadlock to manifest.) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
