stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 5 of 5) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: CS301 Lecture Slides: Concurrency & Deadlocks) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Slide 5: Starvation Mitigation via Aging) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* /F2 10 Tf (    "Aging gradually increases the priority of processes that wait in the system for a long time.") Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (To resolve starvation caused by priority scheduling algorithms, operating systems implement aging.) Tj T* (Over time, an aging priority scheduler ensures that even the lowest-priority process will eventually) Tj T* (become the highest-priority runnable process and gain access to the required resource.) Tj T* ET
endstream
